{
	"about": "Seconds each test of ror's library takes as a CI job runs it (one test thread, the software adapter, four CPUs). tools/ci/test-shard.mjs deals the tests out to the CI jobs by these times; a test not listed counts as the mean of those listed. A missing or stale time never drops a test, it only makes the jobs less even. To refresh from a CI run: node tools/ci/refresh-weights.mjs --repo <owner>/<name> <run id> (--prune drops tests that are gone).",
	"measured": "A desktop's software adapter held to four CPUs without Roblox content, every test in one process (node tools/ci/test-entry.mjs 0 1 <binary> --test-threads=1), 2026-11-27. A GitHub runner takes about twice as long: the next refresh from a CI run replaces these.",
